From 990f70da1a5f347db0e12795dc2bddb4b766cfcd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:15:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] media: qcom: camss: vfe: Set the camnoc_axi_src clock
 rate

On SM8250 the rate table for the camera NoC AXI clock is attached to
"camnoc_axi_src", while vfe_set_clock_rates() only scales clocks named
"camnoc_axi" or "camnoc_rt_axi". The clock is therefore never set and
stays at 19.2 MHz while streaming.

At that rate the bus cannot drain long lines: RDI capture of full
resolution modes (4208x3120 and 4656x3496 RAW10, about 5.3 KiB per
line) never completes a frame, and the bus reports a CCIF violation
for the write master, while binned modes with shorter lines still
work. Scale "camnoc_axi_src" with the pixel clock like the other
camnoc clocks.

Signed-off-by: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
index 319d19158..8d3cffc28 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
@@ -919,6 +919,7 @@ static int vfe_match_clock_names(struct vfe_device *vfe,
 		!strcmp(clock->name, vfe_lite_name) ||
 		!strcmp(clock->name, "vfe_lite") ||
 		!strcmp(clock->name, "camnoc_axi") ||
+		!strcmp(clock->name, "camnoc_axi_src") ||
 		!strcmp(clock->name, "camnoc_rt_axi"));
 }
 
